From c6966d11dee703af3ad6efe764d59a5b1c0944ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 02:20:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(controllers): preserve actor rendering controls

Retain ignore_lighting and the light_color_multiplier expression from Bedrock render controllers so renderers can reproduce their selected lighting. Preserve material override order as it determines which wildcard or bone-specific expression wins. Defaults keep controllers without those fields lit at their original strength.

Retain immutable render-controller UV offset and scale expressions for
camera-dependent client evaluation. Preserve valid neighboring components
when a UV field is malformed, using native identity defaults for missing
components. Numeric and MoLang expressions remain distinct from the
protocol-side lighting calculation.

Bedrock 1.26.51.1 (protocol 2193) controller parser 141cabf60 initializes
offset components at controller+200/+210 to zero and scale components at
+220/+230 to one. Installed ENTITY vertex DXIL applies normalized UV times
UVAnimation.zw plus UVAnimation.xy. Its material uniform default is
(0,0,1,1). The licensed executable SHA-256 is
537c0aee2e79afbdc94b44b28e00f466ae62bc50e2733d953b430db9dbaa9ee7.
Saved CubeCraft controllers require camera and lifetime expressions;
carry those expressions without assuming that a protocol worker knows
the rendering camera. Native assets and raw exports remain private.
